WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:04.980
<b>Nakatomi Yoka</b>

00:00.550 --> 00:03.360
Okay, why don't you introduce yourself?

00:24.290 --> 00:28.040
<b>Train to the End of the World</b>

02:05.720 --> 02:08.810
Episode 2       Suppose, Maybe, Presumably

02:11.780 --> 02:13.650
Wowie!

02:14.230 --> 02:16.000
Look at all this water!

02:16.000 --> 02:17.480
Is this the Koma River?

02:17.480 --> 02:20.550
So this is what the world 
outside Agano looks like now!

02:20.550 --> 02:22.180
Carefree, aren't we?

02:22.180 --> 02:23.070
Hey, now!

02:23.070 --> 02:24.740
You're such a wet blanket, Akira.

02:25.060 --> 02:26.960
I know you're excited, deep down.

02:26.960 --> 02:29.090
You need to show some more emotion!

02:29.090 --> 02:31.180
How could I possibly be excited?

02:31.180 --> 02:32.340
We left without any notice.

02:32.340 --> 02:34.260
And what's with those hands?

02:34.540 --> 02:35.730
Don't do it.

02:35.730 --> 02:37.030
Stay back!

02:37.030 --> 02:39.170
Tickle, tickle!

02:39.430 --> 02:41.830
C'mon, you two.

02:42.180 --> 02:43.180
<b>We're off on a trip, but
we'll be just fine, so
please don't worry about
us.</b>

02:42.180 --> 02:45.140
<b>m 0 0 l 100 0 100 100 0 100</b>

02:43.180 --> 02:43.680
<b>we'll be just fine, so
please don't worry about
us.
It'd be great if you</b>

02:43.680 --> 02:44.180
<b>please don't worry about
us.
It'd be great if you
could let Reimi-chan and</b>

02:44.180 --> 02:44.680
<b>us.
It'd be great if you
could let Reimi-chan and
Akira-chan's families</b>

02:44.680 --> 02:45.140
<b>It'd be great if you
could let Reimi-chan and
Akira-chan's families
know (^^)</b>

02:45.580 --> 02:47.480
Hey, when are we arriving at Ikebukuro?

02:47.480 --> 02:48.270
Like, tomorrow?

02:48.270 --> 02:50.620
It's somewhere not even the 
Black Leopard caravan can go.

02:50.620 --> 02:52.220
Tomorrow's not happening.

02:52.220 --> 02:52.920
What?

02:52.920 --> 02:55.460
But it only took a little 
over an hour before.

02:55.460 --> 02:57.750
I know everything got all stretched out,

02:57.750 --> 02:59.430
but it can't be <i>that</i> bad now, right?

02:59.430 --> 03:00.680
You're way too optimistic.

03:00.680 --> 03:03.180
It's completely possible that 
if we don't take this seriously,

03:03.180 --> 03:05.900
we could succumb to the elements 
before ever reaching Ikebukuro.

03:05.900 --> 03:06.910
Now, hold on.

03:06.910 --> 03:09.380
Sometimes, you find that 
once you actually get going,

03:09.380 --> 03:11.400
it ends up taking barely any time at all.

03:11.400 --> 03:13.120
Maybe not one day, but like, three?

03:13.120 --> 03:14.610
Not a chance.

03:14.610 --> 03:16.730
It'll take a whole month, at least.

03:16.730 --> 03:17.810
Maybe more!

03:17.810 --> 03:18.700
Two weeks!

03:18.700 --> 03:19.500
Three months!

03:19.500 --> 03:20.320
I know.

03:20.320 --> 03:22.540
I'm sure Shizuru-chan's 
thought about all this.

03:22.540 --> 03:23.600
Let's ask.

03:23.600 --> 03:25.360
Hey, how long's it gonna take?

03:24.890 --> 03:26.150
Don't distract me! It's dangerous!

03:26.440 --> 03:30.140
I mean, Shizuru-chan only 
just learned how to drive.

03:30.140 --> 03:30.650
That must be it.

03:35.310 --> 03:37.850
Shizuru-chan, aren't we going a little fast?

03:41.340 --> 03:43.080
I really think this is too fast.

03:43.080 --> 03:45.190
Can't we go slower?

03:45.190 --> 03:46.370
I'm trying.

03:46.370 --> 03:46.790
What?

03:47.100 --> 03:49.650
I'm trying, but it's not slowing down.

03:49.650 --> 03:51.410
What?!

03:52.790 --> 03:53.590
Curve!

03:53.590 --> 03:55.170
Curve, curve!

03:55.740 --> 03:57.600
Curve again!

03:58.620 --> 04:00.670
Curve, curve, curve!

04:02.720 --> 04:03.680
Sharp curve!

04:04.010 --> 04:07.740
Curve!

04:16.680 --> 04:18.510
I thought I was gonna die.

04:18.510 --> 04:20.320
Now I know what they mean by "memento mori."

04:20.320 --> 04:22.900
Are we going to be okay, Shizuru-chan?

04:22.900 --> 04:23.780
I think so.

04:24.180 --> 04:28.660
This looked a lot easier when 
Zenjiro-san was teaching me.

04:29.000 --> 04:30.480
Zenjiro-san?

04:30.480 --> 04:31.920
He can go back to normal.

04:31.920 --> 04:33.750
But only for five minutes a day.

04:33.750 --> 04:34.530
So I had him teach me.

04:34.530 --> 04:35.380
What?

04:35.380 --> 04:36.140
That's impossible.

04:36.140 --> 04:37.320
I swear, I swear.

04:37.320 --> 04:38.320
He turned into a hottie, too.

04:38.320 --> 04:39.170
A hottie?!

04:39.170 --> 04:41.110
Lying is bad, Shizuru-chan.

04:41.110 --> 04:42.920
I swear it's the truth! Seriously!

04:42.920 --> 04:45.010
How else could I have learned 
to drive a train?

04:45.010 --> 04:48.170
You know Zenjiro-san used to be 
an elite railway worker, right?

04:48.170 --> 04:50.230
I thought that was just a rumor.

04:50.230 --> 04:51.220
So it was true?

04:51.220 --> 04:53.570
What do you mean, "only for five minutes?"

04:53.570 --> 04:55.600
You know how train conductors wear a cap?

04:55.600 --> 04:57.110
He turned back when I put it on him.

04:57.110 --> 04:58.940
Listen to me, Shizuru-chan.

04:58.940 --> 05:00.880
Lying really is a bad thing to do.

05:00.880 --> 05:02.040
I swear, I swear!

05:02.040 --> 05:03.070
Swear it on my life!

05:03.070 --> 05:05.060
That's how I learned to drive this thing!

05:05.060 --> 05:06.250
Trust me!

05:06.250 --> 05:09.540
Actually, is this really the 
right way to Ikebukuro?

05:09.540 --> 05:11.180
We're not going the wrong way, are we?

05:11.180 --> 05:11.690
Huh?

05:12.460 --> 05:14.570
Chichibu's back there, right?

05:14.570 --> 05:16.600
That means Ikebukuro's this way.

05:16.600 --> 05:18.170
Oh, that makes sense.

05:18.170 --> 05:19.070
I see.

05:19.070 --> 05:23.070
You know, they have model scouts 
and butlers in Ikebukuro.

05:23.070 --> 05:25.670
As well as detectives and murderers.

05:25.670 --> 05:29.000
If you don't pay attention, you'll be 
stabbed, run over, and scammed!

05:29.000 --> 05:31.390
Spine-tingling, yet stylish!

05:31.390 --> 05:33.390
That's a very distorted view there.

05:33.390 --> 05:35.090
Make sure you don't get ripped off, either.

05:35.090 --> 05:35.580
What?

05:35.580 --> 05:36.590
Reimi, you've got money?

05:36.590 --> 05:37.860
Sure do!

05:37.860 --> 05:39.160
I've been saving up.

05:39.160 --> 05:39.860
Ah!

05:39.860 --> 05:41.530
Nice! How much?

05:41.530 --> 05:42.940
My piggy bank!

05:42.940 --> 05:43.720
Like 20,000 yen?

05:43.720 --> 05:45.960
Wait, my piggy bank!

05:45.960 --> 05:47.410
What's wrong, Reimi-chan?

05:46.680 --> 05:49.060
My piggy bank's back home...

05:47.410 --> 05:49.060
Ah, she left it at home.

05:49.060 --> 05:50.830
All I've got is 250 yen.

05:50.830 --> 05:51.530
That's rough!

05:51.530 --> 05:52.500
What about you?

05:52.500 --> 05:54.220
How much do you have, Akira?

05:54.220 --> 05:56.580
You won't get any personal 
information out of me.

05:56.580 --> 05:58.030
Let me borrow some money!

05:58.030 --> 05:59.880
I'm not loaning any money.

05:59.880 --> 06:00.870
So cheap!

06:00.870 --> 06:03.500
I've got plenty of cash, 
so I'll let you borrow some.

06:03.500 --> 06:04.150
For real?

06:04.150 --> 06:05.290
Shizuru-chan, my savior!

06:05.290 --> 06:06.220
How much are we talking?

06:06.220 --> 06:09.190
I've got a little over 3,000 yen, 
so 1,000 yen or so.

06:09.190 --> 06:09.950
That's nothing!

06:09.950 --> 06:11.090
No way! It's a lot!

06:11.090 --> 06:12.660
What do they say in times like these?

06:12.660 --> 06:14.690
"If you don't have bread, 
let them eat snacks?"

06:14.690 --> 06:16.500
I think that's slightly off.

06:16.500 --> 06:18.300
"You have to crack a few eggs 
to make an omelet."

06:18.300 --> 06:19.810
That's it. Something like that.

06:19.810 --> 06:20.940
No, that's the answer.

06:20.940 --> 06:22.700
1,250 yen, huh?

06:22.700 --> 06:24.250
What should I buy with this?

06:23.430 --> 06:25.330
I think food would come first.

06:25.330 --> 06:27.450
Oh, I want some boba tea, I think it was?

06:27.450 --> 06:30.580
Also some shrshuruli, and French toast...

06:30.580 --> 06:32.380
I meant something more normal.

06:32.380 --> 06:34.030
Like canned goods, or hardtack.

06:34.030 --> 06:35.540
Ugh, that's boring.

06:35.540 --> 06:37.080
Dream a little bigger, Nadeko-chan.

06:37.080 --> 06:39.490
Well, I mean, we didn't 
bring anything with us.

06:39.490 --> 06:40.150
What?

06:40.150 --> 06:42.050
We came here straight after school.

06:42.800 --> 06:44.340
You're right.

06:44.340 --> 06:46.060
We don't have anything to eat.

06:46.060 --> 06:47.700
I brought <i>some</i> food with me.

06:47.700 --> 06:48.810
Really? Awesome!

06:48.810 --> 06:49.690
Why?

06:49.690 --> 06:51.660
Even I know to prep a little.

06:51.660 --> 06:52.590
Can we see?

06:52.590 --> 06:53.440
Yeah, go ahead.

06:53.440 --> 06:57.460
Packing for survival means the 
bare necessities, as well as...

06:57.460 --> 06:58.220
What's this?

06:58.220 --> 06:59.480
A meditation paddle?

06:59.480 --> 07:00.700
Don't you know?

07:00.700 --> 07:02.330
It's for measuring pasta.

07:02.330 --> 07:03.990
So where's the pasta?

07:03.990 --> 07:05.850
That's Su-chan from <i>NeriAli</i>!

07:05.850 --> 07:06.600
You're right!

07:06.600 --> 07:08.430
Why do you have this, Shizuru-chan?

07:08.430 --> 07:10.390
Oh, I found it at my house.

07:09.020 --> 07:10.390
Let me see, Nadeko-chan.

07:10.390 --> 07:11.620
Can I have it? Pretty please?

07:11.620 --> 07:12.260
Sure, I don't mi—

07:12.260 --> 07:12.850
<i>I</i> do.

07:12.850 --> 07:14.170
She gave it to me.

07:13.380 --> 07:15.560
Stop fighting! Play nice!

07:15.580 --> 07:19.830
<b>Chicken Noodles</b>

07:15.580 --> 07:19.830
<b>Tanaka Rice</b>

07:15.580 --> 07:19.830
<b>Bonito Flakes</b>

07:15.580 --> 07:19.830
<b>Soybeans</b>

07:15.580 --> 07:19.830
<b>Kanpyo</b>

07:15.580 --> 07:19.830
<b>Dashi Base</b>

07:15.830 --> 07:19.060
Shizuru-chan, this was 
the only food in there.

07:19.060 --> 07:19.840
Huh?

07:20.180 --> 07:22.620
I'm sure I brought more than that.

07:22.620 --> 07:23.580
As well as those.

07:23.580 --> 07:25.050
Oh, the bitter melon?

07:25.050 --> 07:26.850
I know it's an Agano specialty,

07:26.850 --> 07:29.420
but I'm not a big fan.

07:30.230 --> 07:32.240
What's wrong with me?!

07:32.240 --> 07:32.940
I got too excited!

07:32.940 --> 07:34.710
Or, well, I got a little confused.

07:34.710 --> 07:36.450
Ah, you get like that sometimes.

07:36.450 --> 07:38.140
I guess you could call it tunnel vision.

07:38.140 --> 07:40.000
It couldn't have been worse timing, really.

07:40.000 --> 07:42.020
Maybe it would've helped if you'd made a list.

07:42.870 --> 07:43.990
Um...

07:44.320 --> 07:47.440
This is everything that we have with us.

07:48.970 --> 07:50.520
You know the real problem?

07:50.520 --> 07:51.580
The real problem?

07:51.980 --> 07:53.370
Undies.

07:53.370 --> 07:54.290
Really?

07:54.290 --> 07:55.120
Undies...

07:55.120 --> 07:57.780
Girls shouldn't be saying... <i>that</i>!

07:57.780 --> 07:58.610
Underwear, then.

07:58.610 --> 07:59.440
That's no better!

07:59.440 --> 08:03.090
It's true that we don't know 
how long it'll be to Ikebukuro.

08:03.090 --> 08:04.570
We're stuck in these clothes?

08:04.570 --> 08:07.910
It's said that Isabella, Queen of Castile, 
made an oath to pray for victory,

08:07.910 --> 08:10.580
and didn't change her undies 
for nine months.

08:10.580 --> 08:13.160
You think we'll find Yoka 
if I don't change mine?

08:13.160 --> 08:14.800
Calm down, Shizuru-chan!

08:14.800 --> 08:16.040
Huh? Oh.

08:16.040 --> 08:18.540
We can buy some when 
we get to Higashi-Agano.

08:18.540 --> 08:20.840
We'll need to stock up on food, as well.

08:20.840 --> 08:22.040
Something that'll keep.

08:22.040 --> 08:23.440
I'm hungry.

08:23.440 --> 08:23.720
Ow!

08:23.720 --> 08:24.950
Do you have a death wish?

08:24.950 --> 08:28.000
The fat, hungry ones always die first 
in survival horror movies.

08:28.000 --> 08:28.820
I'm not fat!

08:28.820 --> 08:30.280
Hold on a little bit.

08:30.280 --> 08:31.480
Just for now.

08:31.480 --> 08:32.820
Hold on, huh?

08:32.820 --> 08:33.870
I'm bad at that...

08:34.720 --> 08:37.700
I bet you were gonna say, 
"Reimi sucks at doing that."

08:37.700 --> 08:39.620
Aw, man. You beat me to it.

08:39.620 --> 08:40.970
Now I don't wanna say it.

08:40.970 --> 08:41.710
Seriously?

08:41.710 --> 08:42.910
Settle down.

08:50.040 --> 08:52.340
Are we at Ikebukuro yet?

08:52.340 --> 08:54.150
Are you going to keep asking that?

08:54.150 --> 08:54.930
What's the problem?

08:54.930 --> 08:56.370
I'm just curious.

08:56.370 --> 08:57.900
Are you stupid or something?

08:59.090 --> 09:02.510
That superior attitude 
of yours is a real problem.

09:02.510 --> 09:04.490
Akira the killer sniveler!

09:04.490 --> 09:07.670
I may have been a crybaby, 
but that was over ten years ago!

09:07.670 --> 09:08.270
Hmph!

09:08.270 --> 09:09.810
Flunking monkey Reimi!

09:09.810 --> 09:11.600
I only got a zero that one time!

09:11.600 --> 09:12.640
And it was a quiz!

09:12.640 --> 09:14.520
Cut it out, both of you!

09:14.520 --> 09:16.990
If you hate me so much, 
you should have just stayed in Agano!

09:16.990 --> 09:18.260
I didn't say I hate you!

09:18.260 --> 09:19.720
Don't put words in my mouth!

09:18.830 --> 09:21.260
Akira-chan. Reimi-chan.

09:19.720 --> 09:21.770
You made the choice to ride this train, too!

09:21.770 --> 09:24.620
If you and Nadeko-chan hadn't hopped on, 
I wouldn't have come!

09:24.620 --> 09:27.420
We just got caught up in 
the moment back then.

09:27.420 --> 09:28.610
We all did.

09:28.610 --> 09:30.510
You didn't <i>have</i> to come, you know.

09:33.640 --> 09:36.300
I was planning to go alone from the start.

09:38.250 --> 09:40.370
Shizuru-chan, you're always so...

09:44.550 --> 09:46.070
The bitter melon...

09:46.070 --> 09:48.660
Is it just me, or is it growing 
even faster than usual?

09:48.990 --> 09:51.060
Also, check out this fog.

09:51.060 --> 09:52.510
Where are we?

09:52.510 --> 09:55.040
Don't tell me we passed Higashi-Agano.

10:05.750 --> 10:07.750
Reimi, you have good eyesight, right?

10:07.750 --> 10:09.350
Do you see something out there?

10:09.350 --> 10:10.930
What, are you trying to scare me?

10:10.930 --> 10:12.120
Out there?

10:12.620 --> 10:15.110
I don't really see anything...

10:15.110 --> 10:15.590
Huh?

10:16.040 --> 10:17.000
What <i>is</i> that?

10:17.000 --> 10:17.810
What?!

10:18.120 --> 10:19.250
Something's coming this way.

10:19.250 --> 10:20.580
What do you mean, "something"?

10:20.580 --> 10:21.590
That's...

10:21.590 --> 10:22.610
It's Komassie!

10:22.610 --> 10:23.560
Komassie?

10:23.560 --> 10:27.150
The plesiosaur said to have been living 
in the Koma River to this very day!

10:31.340 --> 10:32.100
Ah.

10:32.610 --> 10:33.980
It's Komassie.

10:36.250 --> 10:37.940
It's Komassie...

10:48.980 --> 10:51.370
Is that a train?

10:53.230 --> 10:55.710
Who are you folks?

10:55.710 --> 10:56.710
Watch out!

10:56.710 --> 10:58.580
That's gotta be a murderer, here to kill us!

10:58.580 --> 10:59.470
Indeed!

10:59.470 --> 11:03.100
They call me the fiercest serial killer 
across all of the Koma River...

11:03.100 --> 11:04.690
Hey! That's a little rude!

11:08.510 --> 11:10.900
Um, who are you?

11:10.900 --> 11:12.880
My name is of little importance!

11:15.270 --> 11:18.530
Or, well, um... I mean...

11:18.530 --> 11:22.860
I've been traveling up the Koma River, 
jotting down notes and doing research.

11:22.860 --> 11:26.060
I haven't seen anyone in ages, 
so you took me by surprise.

11:26.060 --> 11:28.270
Anyway, what are you doing here?

11:28.270 --> 11:31.350
Um, we're trying to get to Ikebukuro.

11:31.350 --> 11:32.760
Huh, Ikebukuro?

11:32.760 --> 11:33.470
Now that's something.

11:33.470 --> 11:35.430
I'm from Ikebukuro myself.

11:35.430 --> 11:36.540
I admire your courage—

11:36.540 --> 11:37.280
Seriously?!

11:37.500 --> 11:39.610
Ikebukuro? That's amazing!

11:39.610 --> 11:41.710
Naw, it's not a big deal.

11:41.710 --> 11:44.390
I've never met anyone from Ikebukuro before!

11:44.390 --> 11:45.640
Oh, really?

11:45.640 --> 11:48.200
Do you know Seibu? Tobu? 
Naka-Ikebukuro Park?

11:48.200 --> 11:49.710
The Ikebus? Animate?

11:49.710 --> 11:51.560
Junkudo? Sanseido?

11:51.560 --> 11:52.570
Also, boba tea!

11:52.570 --> 11:54.150
What's the hottest café right now?

11:54.350 --> 11:55.470
Dunno.

11:55.470 --> 11:56.360
"Dunno"?!

11:56.360 --> 11:57.110
So he has no idea.

11:58.210 --> 11:59.430
Hold it!

11:59.430 --> 12:02.760
There's one thing I can 
say for sure, probably.

12:02.760 --> 12:04.060
What is it?

12:04.320 --> 12:06.490
After the 7G incident,

12:06.490 --> 12:10.350
the whole world disappeared, other than 
everything along the Seibu Ikebukuro line.

12:10.350 --> 12:11.010
What?!

12:11.010 --> 12:14.370
Or so I suppose, maybe, 
as a matter of presumption.

12:14.370 --> 12:16.840
Suppose, maybe, presumably?

12:16.840 --> 12:17.820
Which is it, then?!

12:17.820 --> 12:20.630
The fungi to the east tower high overhead,

12:20.630 --> 12:22.690
brazenly conspiring to subjugate.

12:22.690 --> 12:24.170
Further yet to the east,

12:24.170 --> 12:28.630
those in harmony with goats, untrue to their 
name, charge recklessly as wild boars!

12:28.630 --> 12:29.850
So what does that mean?

12:29.850 --> 12:30.590
What's he saying?

12:30.590 --> 12:31.420
I know what this is.

12:31.420 --> 12:33.320
A poor imitation of a monologue 
from absurdist theater.

12:33.320 --> 12:34.240
Oh, I see.

12:34.240 --> 12:36.500
Is that why it feels so exaggerated?

12:36.500 --> 12:37.740
We should get going.

12:37.740 --> 12:38.330
Huh?

12:38.330 --> 12:40.250
Hey, wait, wait! Please!

12:40.250 --> 12:44.400
My point is, I wouldn't head 
toward Ikebukuro if I were you!

12:44.400 --> 12:45.390
Why not?

12:45.390 --> 12:49.870
It's awfully, terribly, unbelievably bad 
out there, I hear, supposedly!

12:49.870 --> 12:51.320
Or so you presume.

12:51.320 --> 12:52.340
Yep.

12:52.790 --> 12:53.660
Okay, off we go.

12:53.660 --> 12:54.630
Hey, wait!

12:55.220 --> 12:57.740
Since you came all this way, 
give me something!

12:57.740 --> 12:59.840
Pretty please!

13:00.810 --> 13:02.800
I'll give you something good! Real good!

13:02.800 --> 13:03.670
Let's trade!

13:03.670 --> 13:04.670
Something good?

13:04.670 --> 13:06.640
I drew this map myself.

13:06.640 --> 13:07.860
It'll totally be helpful.

13:07.860 --> 13:08.850
I super recommend it.

13:08.850 --> 13:10.350
Ah, thanks.

13:10.350 --> 13:11.560
Also, a word of advice.

13:11.560 --> 13:13.080
Don't believe anything you hear.

13:13.080 --> 13:13.800
Huh?

13:13.800 --> 13:16.810
Believe only the things 
you've confirmed yourself.

13:16.810 --> 13:18.310
Oh, that doesn't apply to what I say.

13:18.800 --> 13:19.880
Myself...

13:21.820 --> 13:24.650
This guy's talking the very 
definition of nonsense.

13:24.650 --> 13:27.180
Ow, that stings!

13:27.180 --> 13:28.170
Shizuru-chan.

13:28.170 --> 13:29.750
Why don't you give him this?

13:29.750 --> 13:30.690
I think it's your dad's.

13:30.980 --> 13:32.380
It's not like we need it.

13:32.380 --> 13:33.200
M-My word!

13:33.200 --> 13:36.150
That great modern convenience, 
a heated tobacco device!

13:36.150 --> 13:37.660
Well, the cartridge!

13:37.660 --> 13:39.460
If you're happy with that, it's yours.

13:39.460 --> 13:42.460
Thank you! Merci! Grazie! Khop khun kha!

13:42.460 --> 13:43.780
You're welcome.

13:43.780 --> 13:45.440
Take care, gramps.

13:45.440 --> 13:46.590
Leave it to me!

13:46.590 --> 13:50.530
I'll go up the Koma River, studying and 
exploring along the Seibu Ikebukuro line,

13:50.530 --> 13:52.480
solving all the mysteries...

13:52.480 --> 13:53.590
Wait, hold on.

13:53.590 --> 13:55.590
Don't call me "gramps"!

13:55.590 --> 13:56.990
I'm still young!

13:57.830 --> 13:59.550
He sure was a weirdo.

13:59.550 --> 14:02.700
It's the first time in a while we've 
met a human grown-up, though.

14:02.700 --> 14:04.020
Other than Neko-san and his crew.

14:04.020 --> 14:05.480
Oh, that's true.

14:05.790 --> 14:08.950
He kinda looked like he should 
be selling talismans.

14:08.950 --> 14:10.100
Oh, I can see it.

14:10.100 --> 14:11.710
The shady and totally bogus ones.

14:11.710 --> 14:14.950
That's the first time I've met someone 
weirder than Zenjiro-san.

14:14.950 --> 14:16.310
That reminds me.

14:16.310 --> 14:18.440
Why didn't Zenjiro-san come with us?

14:18.440 --> 14:20.060
Ew. I don't want him here.

14:20.060 --> 14:21.060
Where would he sleep?

14:21.060 --> 14:23.740
You're being a little too superficial here.

14:23.740 --> 14:26.600
If he was here, we could ask him 
all sorts of things.

14:26.600 --> 14:28.940
Zenjiro-san said he didn't 
want to leave Agano.

14:28.940 --> 14:29.970
He couldn't leave.

14:29.970 --> 14:31.200
Why not?

14:31.200 --> 14:35.770
Whenever he tries to leave Agano, 
he gets really nasty headaches and vertigo.

14:35.770 --> 14:38.360
He said it's because of the 
wibble-wobble surgery.

14:38.360 --> 14:39.920
What if it's psychological suggestion?

14:39.920 --> 14:41.020
Suggestion?

14:41.020 --> 14:43.020
Like brainwashing or hypnosis?

14:43.020 --> 14:43.750
Yeah.

14:43.750 --> 14:47.320
What if that wibble-wobble state of his 
is just a form of suggestion,

14:47.320 --> 14:49.320
and there's no actual basis to any of it?

14:49.600 --> 14:52.580
He <i>does</i> have a scar on his forehead, though.

14:52.580 --> 14:54.190
That's true.

14:54.190 --> 14:57.770
Well, anyway, I'm glad Zenjiro-san's not here.

14:57.770 --> 14:59.340
Oh, Reimi-chan.

14:59.340 --> 15:02.000
Another person would mean 
less food for us, too.

15:02.650 --> 15:07.160
On that note, Shizuru-chan, 
why did <i>you</i> decide to go to Ikebukuro?

15:07.160 --> 15:10.610
When you come right 
out and ask like that...

15:10.610 --> 15:12.290
It was for Yoka-chan, right?

15:13.140 --> 15:15.220
Just because you couldn't find her 
anywhere near Agano?

15:15.500 --> 15:17.820
Reimi, do you have to say it like that?

15:17.820 --> 15:19.280
What? It's true.

15:19.280 --> 15:20.470
Isn't it, Shizuru-chan?

15:20.840 --> 15:22.760
Well, yeah.

15:22.760 --> 15:24.720
Because you saw that photo in the newspaper?

15:24.720 --> 15:26.980
Yeah, something like that.

15:27.280 --> 15:29.260
How are you going to find her?

15:29.260 --> 15:30.280
Doesn't seem likely.

15:30.280 --> 15:31.340
You never know.

15:31.340 --> 15:33.100
Maybe as soon as we reach Ikebukuro,

15:33.100 --> 15:36.290
Yoka-chan will come up to us 
and go, "Long time no see!"

15:36.290 --> 15:37.320
Yeah, totally.

15:37.320 --> 15:39.050
Wouldn't that be nice.

15:39.940 --> 15:41.880
You know, Shizuru-chan.

15:41.880 --> 15:45.550
If you'd left Agano without 
saying anything to us,

15:45.550 --> 15:51.780
you could have ended up making us sad, 
just like when Yoka-chan disappeared on you.

15:51.780 --> 15:53.340
Oh, huh.

15:53.340 --> 15:55.320
I didn't think about that.

15:55.320 --> 15:55.750
Sorry.

15:57.020 --> 15:59.210
Let's have you apologize for one more thing.

15:59.210 --> 15:59.590
Huh?

16:00.250 --> 16:03.690
For suggesting we shouldn't have come along.

16:06.960 --> 16:08.060
Sorry.

16:08.970 --> 16:12.820
Yoka-chan is our friend too, you know.

16:13.120 --> 16:14.070
Yeah.

16:15.070 --> 16:17.100
C'mon, isn't that enough?

16:17.100 --> 16:18.440
No, I really am sorry.

16:18.440 --> 16:20.300
I wasn't thinking about your feelings.

16:20.630 --> 16:22.320
As long as you understand now.

16:22.320 --> 16:23.090
Yep, yep!

16:23.090 --> 16:25.000
Now that that's settled, 
let's head back to Agano.

16:25.000 --> 16:25.640
Huh?!

16:26.120 --> 16:27.310
Are you stupid?

16:27.310 --> 16:29.130
What are you saying, Reimi-chan?

16:29.130 --> 16:31.050
Huh? We need to prepare properly.

16:31.050 --> 16:34.430
Clothes, food, blankets, camping gear.

16:34.430 --> 16:37.330
Oh, wouldn't some scented candles be great?

16:37.330 --> 16:38.170
Oh.

16:38.170 --> 16:39.120
They would.

16:39.120 --> 16:40.880
Not getting enough sleep causes stress.

16:40.880 --> 16:42.420
Wait, hold on.

16:42.420 --> 16:43.610
Go back after coming this far?

16:43.610 --> 16:44.490
Isn't that a waste?

16:44.490 --> 16:48.120
I can't help but worry about 
our lack of supplies, though.

16:48.120 --> 16:52.120
Wait, I never agreed 
to this trip to begin with.

16:52.120 --> 16:55.770
When we go back to Agano, 
you can stay behind by yourself, then.

16:55.770 --> 16:57.620
I don't want to be all by myself!

17:07.420 --> 17:10.250
Koyuki-san, sorry to make you do all this.

17:10.250 --> 17:14.150
In that case, I want to bring 
<i>Prince Takaoka's Travels</i>.

17:14.150 --> 17:14.850
What's that?

17:14.850 --> 17:16.640
A novel. You wouldn't have heard of it.

17:16.640 --> 17:17.480
Oh, yeah?

17:17.480 --> 17:21.390
Then I'm bringing jalapeño chips, 
which I know you can't eat.

17:21.390 --> 17:22.760
They're so good.

17:22.760 --> 17:25.050
We'll need to submit absence letters, too.

17:25.050 --> 17:28.500
Or should it be a longer leave of absence?

17:28.500 --> 17:30.660
All right! I'm gonna start her up!

17:43.360 --> 17:44.410
What's going on?

17:44.980 --> 17:47.120
It wasn't like this before.

17:47.380 --> 17:49.130
The water level's risen.

17:49.130 --> 17:49.980
But why?

17:49.980 --> 17:50.720
The map!

17:50.720 --> 17:52.600
The one from that shady hermit!

17:59.620 --> 18:00.590
What's that sound?

18:04.400 --> 18:05.530
Ah, Morse.

18:05.530 --> 18:07.120
This is Morse code.

18:07.120 --> 18:07.870
Ah!

18:07.870 --> 18:09.810
I forgot I asked Grandma Koyuki!

18:09.810 --> 18:10.910
To send us Morse code?

18:10.910 --> 18:12.070
No, no.

18:12.070 --> 18:13.230
Zenjiro-san.

18:13.230 --> 18:14.800
They're not responding!

18:14.800 --> 18:17.480
We promised to contact each other 
at 5:00 p.m. every day!

18:17.890 --> 18:20.350
Agano here! Please respond!

18:22.820 --> 18:24.250
Huh? What?

18:24.250 --> 18:25.790
Dot dash dash?

18:25.540 --> 18:27.870
<b>Japanese Morse Code</b>

18:25.790 --> 18:27.070
A little slower...

18:27.070 --> 18:28.700
What was "A" again?

18:33.920 --> 18:34.770
So fast!

18:34.770 --> 18:35.640
Is that right?

18:35.640 --> 18:36.790
You're not just making it up?

18:36.790 --> 18:37.640
Shut up.

18:40.300 --> 18:41.990
"Water level rising"?

18:41.990 --> 18:43.320
Do they mean the Koma River?

18:43.900 --> 18:47.260
"Motor flooding dangerous. 
Flee to higher ground."

18:47.260 --> 18:47.940
So he says.

18:47.940 --> 18:49.080
What?!

18:49.080 --> 18:51.250
Wait, no, which way do we go?

18:51.250 --> 18:52.210
We're in trouble!

18:52.210 --> 18:53.020
Hold it.

18:53.020 --> 18:54.810
Spoken verbiage doesn't work here.

18:54.810 --> 18:56.810
Advance or retreat? Please advise.

18:58.660 --> 19:03.540
"GSI surveys say Agano and Higashi-Agano's 
elevations choo-choo choo..."

19:03.540 --> 19:04.490
"Choo"?

19:05.000 --> 19:06.440
Our five minutes are up!

19:06.440 --> 19:07.690
What do we do, Shizuru-chan?

19:26.220 --> 19:29.080
Forward!

19:32.660 --> 19:33.530
It's coming!

19:33.530 --> 19:34.510
It's right behind us!

19:34.510 --> 19:36.270
Calm down, calm down!

19:44.530 --> 19:45.290
Faster!

19:45.290 --> 19:46.470
Go faster!

19:46.470 --> 19:47.790
I'm trying!

19:56.170 --> 19:57.030
Forward!

19:57.030 --> 19:58.090
Let's go!

19:58.090 --> 20:01.300
Move!

20:20.520 --> 20:22.190
We can't go back.

20:23.420 --> 20:25.040
But, well, it's for the best.

20:25.370 --> 20:26.420
How so?

20:26.420 --> 20:27.780
Now we have to keep going.

20:28.550 --> 20:29.460
Yeah.

20:29.920 --> 20:32.060
What about those scented candles?

20:32.060 --> 20:34.190
They can wait until we get to Ikebukuro.

20:34.190 --> 20:35.340
I thought you only had one thousand yen.

20:35.340 --> 20:36.950
Let me borrow some money.

20:36.950 --> 20:37.420
No.

20:37.420 --> 20:38.440
I'm not loaning any money.

20:38.440 --> 20:39.140
So stingy!

20:39.140 --> 20:39.890
Hey!

20:41.310 --> 20:43.640
Are we really going to Ikebukuro?

20:44.560 --> 20:45.560
Looks like it.

20:45.560 --> 20:47.820
It's our only option now.

20:47.820 --> 20:48.850
What about you?

20:50.530 --> 20:51.570
I'm going.

20:51.570 --> 20:53.410
I'll go and find Yoka!

21:45.430 --> 21:47.850
It's Higashi-Agano!

21:54.210 --> 21:55.470
Hey there.

21:55.470 --> 21:57.050
Welcome to Higashi-Agano.

21:57.050 --> 21:59.120
We don't get many visitors here.

21:59.120 --> 22:00.900
I'll say.

22:02.140 --> 22:05.000
Please, feel free to rest a while here.
